---
alwaysApply: true
---

Follow `AGENTS.md` in the project root for the full rule set.

- Work on one `TASKS.md` item at a time. Prefer small diffs.
- After a behavior change, run the project test command if one exists (usually `npm test` when `package.json` has a `test` script). Do not start the next task until tests pass. Do not delete or weaken tests to make a task look done.
- Commit only after a successful milestone. The remote is `nico-wood/campus-call`. Do not run `git init` again. Never commit `.env`, `.env.*`, API keys, tokens, or passwords.
- Vercel project `campus-call` is on the `nico-wood` Hobby team. Do not run `vercel --prod`. Supabase and skill choices are in `SETUP.md`.
- Keep secrets in gitignored env files or the host's environment variables. Never print them in logs, commits, or `PROGRESS.md`.
- After each milestone or failed retry, append what happened to `PROGRESS.md`. Retry a failing task at most 3 times, then log and move on.
- If a milestone should be visible on a preview URL and the project is already linked to a host, deploy a preview. If it is not linked, note that and skip.
- Stay inside this project folder.
